# Meathook Massacre II cast for X = 1 (six mana: a Black Lotus, a Mox Jet and two more Moxen for {1}{1}{B}{B}{B}{B}):
# "each player sacrifices X creatures of their choice" (CR 701.21a, 101.4). Bot1 sacrifices a Memnite, keeping its Ornithopter,
# and Bot2 an Ornithopter, keeping its Memnite. Both deaths trigger: Bot1 "may pay 3 life" for its own creature and does
# (17 life), so its Memnite comes back under its control with a finality counter on it; Bot2 "may pay 3 life" for its
# Ornithopter and declines (20 life), so Bot1 gets that Ornithopter, with a finality counter, under its control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Memnite
Ornithopter
Meathook Massacre II
Lightning Bolt
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Ornithopter
Island x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Meathook Massacre II.Cast(X: 1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Memnite)
Bot2.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot2.Decline
Bot1.Accept
? Bot1.Life = 17
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Counters.Finality = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = false
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 17
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Exile.Memnite.Power = 1
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Black Lotus
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield = Memnite
